            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital admission of your 88-year-old male patient from 25/07/2020 to 26/07/2020. He presented with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, exhibiting significant dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed the exacerbation. He was commenced on supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, and a course of systemic corticosteroids. Blood tests were performed to exclude secondary causes. He responded well to treatment with notable clinical improvement. He is discharged home with optimised inhaler therapy and a short steroid taper. I recommend close follow-up in your practice and would suggest pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you have any questions. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>
               </text>
